// KEYSTONE BRIDGE (new) — the company-brain router proved with ZERO auth.
//
// Given only a UK postcode, Orbital:
//   1. calls Postcodes.io to resolve the postcode -> Latitude / Longitude
//   2. feeds those coordinates into Police.uk to fetch street crime
//
// Orbital is never told Postcodes.io and Police.uk are connected. It discovers the
// path because both bind the same uk.gov.Latitude / uk.gov.Longitude types. This one
// new adapter (Postcodes.io) is the single edge that fuses the ORG cluster (Companies
// House emits a Postcode) to the GEO cluster (Police / Flood / TfL).
//
// EC2R 8AH = Monzo Bank's registered office.
given { pc : uk.gov.Postcode = "EC2R 8AH" }
find { uk.gov.apis.police_uk.StreetCrime[] }
